WEBVTT

00:02:28.978 --> 00:02:30.688
and that I was not alone.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.360
It was an experience I never forgot.

00:02:36.944 --> 00:02:39.030
And many years later,

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:43.910
after I became a data science professor
at the University of Washington

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.871
in 2013,

00:02:46.871 --> 00:02:50.208
I met another professor named Katie Davis,

00:02:50.208 --> 00:02:51.709
and we sat down over lunch

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:53.586
and discussed a recent news story

00:02:53.586 --> 00:02:57.298
that claimed “kids today can’t write,

00:02:57.298 --> 00:03:00.259
all they produce
is misspelled short texts.”